====== BT Home Hub 2.0 Type A ======
{{:media:bt:homehub2a-cover.png?nolink&200x150}}

These black boxes were given away with a BT broadband subscription.  They comes in two variants labelled Type A and Type B.  The two look identical, and although they provide the same functionality, they are very different on the inside.

  * This type (Type A) is made by Thomson, and is Broadcom-based, shipping with a Linux-based firmware and a custom bootloader.  The bootloader can be replaced by a standard [[docs:techref:bootloader:cfe|CFE]] allowing OpenWrt to be flashed/run.
  * [[toh/bt/homehub_v2b|Type B]] is made by SHC (Siemens), and is Infineon/Lantiq Danube based, shipping with an OpenRG-based Linux firmware.  The bootloader is U-Boot.

Both include ADSL2+, 802.11b/g/n wireless, one USB 2.0 host port, 4 10/100 wired ethernet ports, DECT, FXS & FXO ports and VOIP functionality.

